[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The few tables no narrative can hold are computed by one registered query module

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-QUERIES
TITLE: The few tables no narrative can hold are computed by one registered query module
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A narrative can draw over what it contains or names with Over. Three
things no narrative can name by relation without breaking the plan-refs
rule: the roots of every view in the canon, every node of the canon, and a
type's live counts over the whole export. A widget whose subject is one of
those names a query word in its TAGS (roots, nodes, grammar), and one
registered module computes the table into the payload. The list of query
words is closed and small; a new one is a canon decision and a script edit.
<<<
